{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876995-how-common-are-solar-marriages","id":876995,"title":"How common are Solar marriages?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-28T14:48:13-07:00","id":876995,"title":"How common are Solar marriages?","content":"So I realized an interesting pattern among fluff Solars recently, that being that it is very rare to see romantic relationships between Solars. The only two examples that I could find were Desus &amp; Bright (not exactly a healthy relationship) , Alkadi &amp; Luthe's admin (clearly stated as a marriage of convenience) &amp; Gold-Shadowed Arrow and his lover (who dont seem to be wed either). So do you think that Solars rarely bonded romantically or that they were merely not mentioned frequently? Also do you think that they were predisposed towards unhealthy relationships (of those only Jades predecessor seemed to be remotely healthy)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 04-28-2016, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T14:50:01-07:00","id":876997,"title":"","content":"It's Gold-<i>Shadowed</i> Arrow.<br /> <br /> Also, what about Swan and Arianna?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T14:54:35-07:00","id":877000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876995-how-common-are-solar-marriages?p=876997#post876997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's Gold-<i>Shadowed</i> Arrow.<br /> <br /> Also, what about Swan and Arianna?</div> </div> </div> </div>My mistake. Well I tend to put them in the same slot as their previous incarnations since the caste books talked heavily about how much it factored in. Also with her behaviour that one also seems unhealthy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T15:12:23-07:00","id":877011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876995-how-common-are-solar-marriages?p=877000#post877000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also with her behaviour that one also seems unhealthy...</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh? Not sure I get you there\u2026<br /> <br /> Also, there's quite a load of difference between a marriage and a romantic relationship and a healthy relationship; shit, some of the least-healthy, least-romantic relationships I've seen have been in married couples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-28-2016, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T15:16:06-07:00","id":877015,"title":"","content":"Sometimes Solars are romantically involved with other Solars. Sometimes not. Does it really matter if it's the norm or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/922-hailey-mcauliffe","name":"Hailey McAuliffe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T16:04:51-07:00","id":877047,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.<br /> <br /> Let's see.<br /> <br /> Right now, I have three active Solars in games. One's with a Dragonblood, one's in the early stages of puppy love with <i>a</i> Lunar who might or might not be <i>her</i> Lunar, and the third is desperately attempting to hang on to her relationship with her girlfriend, Arianna.<br /> <br /> Not that Rashi would be particularly <i>threatened</i> by having Blood Apes summoned to kill her - again - but that would mean Sad Arianna, and she doesn't want <i>that</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T16:19:46-07:00","id":877064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hailey McAuliffe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876995-how-common-are-solar-marriages?p=877015#post877015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes Solars are romantically involved with other Solars. Sometimes not. Does it really matter if it's the norm or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh it is most definitely not the norm, I just find it interesting that the Solars of the First Age didnt seem to like having partners among the only group that they deemed their equal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T16:35:42-07:00","id":877080,"title":"","content":"I think Solars as people are infrequent enough that any of their activities need to be considered as self-contained things rather than evidence of prevailing trends.<br /> <br /> Soooo... <i>technically</i> Solar marriages to other Solars are going to be rare, but that's because Solar relationships of all kinds are rare. It doesn't really demonstrate anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T16:37:41-07:00","id":877082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876995-how-common-are-solar-marriages?p=877064#post877064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh it is most definitely not the norm, I just find it interesting that the Solars of the First Age didnt seem to like having partners among the only group that they deemed their equal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said it in another thread, but I'll say it here as well: the closest companions and confidantes of kings were seldom other kings - more typically, it was the slaves and servants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-28-2016, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T16:40:13-07:00","id":877085,"title":"","content":"Well yeah. I mean, marrying another Solar might get you a lifetime of matrimonial bliss, but marrying a Sidereal gets you <i>a bigger mote pool</i>.<br /> <br /> It's not even a contest, am I right, gentlemen?<br /> <br /> *points* This guy knows what I'm talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T16:43:15-07:00","id":877088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876995-how-common-are-solar-marriages?p=877064#post877064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh it is most definitely not the norm, I just find it interesting that the Solars of the First Age didnt seem to like having partners among the only group that they deemed their equal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it might be Observation Bias; ordinary Solar-Solar pairings would be, in general, less 'interesting' from a storytelling perspective than Solar-Something Else, and so we simply don't see them in the writeups. if, for instance, in - say - 10 couples 8 are quiet Solar/Solar but the other two are Solar/Infernal and Solar/Abyssal then you hear about those two, and the rest don't get spoken of and thus seem not to exist...<br /> <br /> Of course, my Night Caste Solar is an incorrigible flirt who (openly) disdains the idea of getting tied down (&quot;as opposed to up&quot;) but (internally) has a variety of self-doubts (&quot;I'd make a TERRIBLE mother&quot;) and who, in two different games at different points on what can, with squinting, be considered the same timeline (think of it as like the Aligned Continuity in Transformers), is in the first the sort who drunkenly called a Queen &quot;sugartits&quot; and got away with it, and in the set-later game recently found her Lunar and is very confused by the feelings she feels for her, and it doesn't help that said Lunar is 1. First Age vintage and 2. <i>completely loco</i> in a (mostly) functioning way because the Solar's Past Life was The Being <i>Now</i> Known As The Lover Clad In The Raiment Of Tears...<br /> <br /> (My other main character (in another party within the second game) is a Looksyan Wood Aspect who has - entirely unplannedly - gone <i>utterly head-over-heels</i> for the party Twilight.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6118,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6118-thebushranger","user":"TheBushranger","date":". 04-28-2016, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6118-thebushranger","name":"TheBushranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T17:12:20-07:00","id":877125,"title":"","content":"Probably quite rare, considering that Lunars were the preferred mates of Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T17:36:02-07:00","id":877155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876995-how-common-are-solar-marriages?p=877080#post877080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Solars as people are infrequent enough that any of their activities need to be considered as self-contained things rather than evidence of prevailing trends.<br /> <br /> Soooo... <i>technically</i> Solar marriages to other Solars are going to be rare, but that's because Solar relationships of all kinds are rare. It doesn't really demonstrate anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason the last few times I'd viewed this thread, your post wasn't showing up, but now that I see it I'm throwing my Like at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T17:51:39-07:00","id":877165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876995-how-common-are-solar-marriages?p=877082#post877082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said it in another thread, but I'll say it here as well: the closest companions and confidantes of kings were seldom other kings - more typically, it was the slaves and servants.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bDarn it, this is making me think of... something, some fiction I can't remember in which attention was drawn to the pathos inherent to the point that the protagonist and antagonist were figures of major authority and extremely intimate rivals despite the fact that they never actually meet physically or directly exchange words...<br /> <br /> Or maybe it was a couple of things... a combination of Wrath of Khan (Kirk and Khan do exchange some words, but never share screen time) and the Smiley versus Karla series of John La Carre.<br /> <br /> (One of my favourite parts of the film of Tinker Tailor Soldier Spy is when Smiley recalls the one time he met Karla, but admits he doesn't remember what he looked like, and then it comes back at the end to say that from that brief meeting Karla was able to glean major details of Smiley's personality that he could incorporate into managing operations decades later.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T18:46:31-07:00","id":877212,"title":"","content":"Leviathans Solar mate in the first age, Admiral Arkade I believe was his name, was married to another Solar. Who Leviathan was having an affair with.<br /> <br /> Now if you think about it. A Solar doesn't have a lot of options in the dating pool. Sure they could marry a mortal and have them drop dead in a blink of an eye compared to the long lives that Solars can live, assuming they don't get themselves killed. But realistically, any Solar or other exalted of any real age is most likely going to gravitate towards mates who are similarly long lived.<br /> <br /> If you think about it watching everyone around you grow old and die, while you remain young and strong, can be very isolating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4498-ardis","name":"Ardis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T18:52:42-07:00","id":877217,"title":"","content":"Still not sure what you mean about Arianna and Swan being unhealthy, OP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T19:08:42-07:00","id":877230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876995-how-common-are-solar-marriages?p=877217#post877217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still not sure what you mean about Arianna and Swan being unhealthy, OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Namely it seems that it is extremely one-sided with Arianna thinking of Swan as a sidekick. I hesitate to really call it a romantic relationship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T19:59:45-07:00","id":877262,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Blooded and mortals were considered to be more pets or toys to First Age Solar Exalted than proper mates from what I understand, so I doubt that they would have married them that often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T20:07:36-07:00","id":877267,"title":"","content":"Medieval lords married mediaval noblewomen, even though those women had little in terms of rights.<br /> <br /> Marriage as a union of equals is an ideal that many cultures in history just didn't consider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-28-2016, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T13:48:10-07:00","id":878064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876995-how-common-are-solar-marriages?p=877267#post877267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Medieval lords married mediaval noblewomen, even though those women had little in terms of rights.<br /> <br /> Marriage as a union of equals is an ideal that many cultures in history just didn't consider.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They did it because their children were supposed to inherit their titles and holdings. Because of their life spam, Exalted social dynamics is a bit different.<br /> <br /> PS: Exalted who finds herself in love with a mortal goes out on epic quest to give said mortal some kind of immortality or extended life spam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T15:07:18-07:00","id":878140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876995-how-common-are-solar-marriages?p=877230#post877230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Namely it seems that it is extremely one-sided with Arianna thinking of Swan as a sidekick. I hesitate to really call it a romantic relationship.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you go by Scroll of Exalts, sure, but SoE also doesn't understand the scale of the world when it comes to Arianna's back story, so I'd chuck that detail post-haste. You might conceivably have a reason for having a character who was born in the middle of the Scavenger Lands fuck off some place up North, but if they're doing it to find an academic institution, they probably wouldn't even have to leave the Hundred Kingdoms area. Better to have Arianna born in the place up north and have lived there for a long time before realizing how small it was after her Exaltation, which is what her writeup in the CB:T suggested. Among other things, such as a much less conceited opinion of Swan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}